RFC 007: Resource Foraging, Weight, Skills & Carrying Capacity Spec
Status: Draft / Proposed
Target Stack: Pure Go, Mochi-MQTT, SQLite, RKLLM

1. Executive Summary & Weight Invariants
RFC 007 establishes the physical resource foraging engine, metric mass (kg) carrying capacity, skill-based progression, and spatial inventory constraints for Agentville. Item transport and physical limits are strictly enforced by the server. Carrying limits directly dictate energy expenditure, movement permissions, and trade logistics.

2. Carrying Capacity & Container Gear
Base unassisted carrying capacity is 20.0 kg. Exceeding capacity imposes server-enforced encumbrance penalties:
- 0.0 kg – 20.0 kg (Unencumbered): Standard movement speed and baseline energy decay.
- 20.1 kg – 30.0 kg (Encumbered): Double energy decay per action tick.
- > 30.0 kg (Overburdened): Movement intents (MOVE) are strictly rejected by the server until excess weight is relieved.

